    "body": "- [ ] I, the PR author, have personally reviewed every line of this PR.\n\n## What does this PR do?\n\nTemporarily disable `hybrid_llama3_proxy_mfsdp_v2_cuda_graph` in the H100 development MR and GitHub merge-queue suites by changing its scopes to `mr-broken` and `mr-github-broken`.\n\nTwo queue jobs reproduce the same validation failure in all three attempts: only metric steps 1–3 are available against 50 golden steps, despite training stdout reaching iteration 50. This blocks queue entries on loss and memory checks. The test, configuration, and golden values remain available for investigation and re-enabling.\n\n## Issue tracking\n\nRelated to #8218. This quarantine does not resolve the underlying metric logging/extraction issue; keep the issue open until the test can be re-enabled.\n\n## Validation\n\n- Parsed the YAML and verified that only this test's two scopes change; all other recipe data is identical.\n- `git diff --check` passed.\n- `BASE_REF=main CHECK_ONLY=true SKIP_DOCS=false bash tools/autoformat.sh` passed (no Python changes).\n- GPU tests were not run for this scheduling-only change.\n\n## Contribution process\n\n- [x] I have run the repository autoformatter check.\n- No new unit/functional tests, typing, or kernel coverage are applicable to this recipe quarantine.\n",
